{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Overall Guidelines\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab The exam will be in class, paper and pen (no pencils, please - they smudge!). No computers will be used or needed. Write legibly.{\super\chftn}{\*\footnote\chftn\~\plain\pard {\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 I\u8217'll try to decipher everything, but ultimately, if I can\u8217't read it, it can\u8217't earn points.\par}
}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab The exam will have two sections - IDs and short answer.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab An \u8220"ID\u8221", or identification, question, simply gives you a term and asks you to define it and identify its relevance for the study of AI and AI Policy.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab A short answer is like a short essay - nothing terribly long, but should be structured, potentially with short paragraphs. You could also be given a news article or data graphic about AI and be asked to interpret and situate it, saying why it is important to the broader discussion of AI.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab I do not imagine the exam will take the entire class period, but you will have the entire class period to complete it.\sa180\par}
